; Phonemes in, one segment record of 11 cards out for each phoneme and pause: pc s wf pms send kind inh mn cls9
; liq vls. A phoneme card is 10 x code + stress; -1 is a word boundary, -2 a comma, -3 a period, -4 a question
; mark, -5 an exclamation mark, -9 the end. For each record it asks the host for row pc of the phoneme table (OUT
; at 21; a pause is pc 0, whose row is kind 8) and copies the row's first six cards (kind inh mn cls9 liq vls). A
; pause's record has its length in ms (300 for a comma, else 600) and whether it ends a sentence (send 1, or 2 for
; a question). A 50 ms pause comes first; a 150 ms pause comes last and ends the last sentence too (send 3). The
; segment after a pause or a boundary starts a word (wf 1). WH's row is W's.
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03            start   CLA   c50      03-05: the pause at the start
  04                    STO   pms
  05                    JMP   rec
  06            loop    INP   t        06-15: a phoneme: pc and s
  07                    CLA   t
  08                    TAC   ctl
  09                    SFT   01
  10                    STO   pc
  11                    SFT   10
  12                    STO   x
  13                    CLA   t
  14                    SUB   x
  15                    STO   s
  16            rec     OUT   pc       16-30: the record, with the table's six cards
  17                    OUT   pc
  18                    OUT   s
  19                    OUT   wf
  20                    OUT   pms
  21                    OUT   snd
  22                    CLA   n5
  23                    STO   i
  24            cp      INP   x
  25                    OUT   x
  26                    CLA   i
  27                    SUB   00
  28                    STO   i
  29                    TAC   nxt
  30                    JMP   cp
  31            nxt     CLA   snd      31-45: stop after the end pause; wf 1 after a pause, else 0
  32                    SUB   n3
  33                    TAC   go
  34                    HRS   00
  35            go      CLA   z
  36                    SUB   pms
  37                    TAC   one
  38                    CLA   z
  39                    JMP   setw
  40            one     CLA   00
  41            setw    STO   wf
  42                    CLA   z
  43                    STO   pms
  44                    STO   snd
  45                    JMP   loop
  46            ctl     CLA   z        46-94: -1, a boundary: the next phoneme starts a word
  47                    STO   pc
  48                    STO   s
  49                    CLA   t
  50                    ADD   00
  51                    TAC   pa
  52                    CLA   00
  53                    STO   wf
  54                    JMP   loop
  55            pa      ADD   00       60-100: -2 to -5 pauses, -9 the end pause
  56                    TAC   p3
  57                    CLA   c300
  58                    STO   pms
  59                    JMP   rec
  60            p3      CLA   c600
  61                    STO   pms
  62                    CLA   t
  63                    ADD   n3
  64                    TAC   p4
  65                    CLA   00
  66                    JMP   sn
  67            p4      ADD   00
  68                    TAC   p5
  69                    CLA   n2
  70                    JMP   sn
  71            p5      ADD   00
  72                    TAC   pend
  73                    CLA   00
  74                    JMP   sn
  75            pend    CLA   c150
  76                    STO   pms
  77                    CLA   n3
  78            sn      STO   snd
  79                    JMP   rec
  80            t       DATA  0
  81            pc      DATA  0
  82            s       DATA  0
  83            wf      DATA  0
  84            pms     DATA  0
  85            snd     DATA  0
  86            x       DATA  0
  87            i       DATA  0
  88            z       DATA  0
  89            c50     DATA  50
  90            n5      DATA  5
  91            n3      DATA  3
  92            n2      DATA  2
  93            c300    DATA  300
  94            c600    DATA  600
  95            c150    DATA  150
